  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam Chamber of Commerce and Industry (VCCI), the most representative employers and business membership organization in Viet Nam needs to strengthen its role as a service provider in the post-pandemic context. This includes strengthening the institutional capacity, developing sustainable service models, and equipping member enterprises with practical tools to meet growing expectations on responsible business conduct (RBC), human rights due diligence (HRDD), and just transition. 
The ILO plays a strategic supporting role by helping design and deliver new services, including operationalizing EMBO&#x2019;s Responsible Business Helpdesk, developing training modules on RBC and HRDD, and supporting enterprise-level training on tools such as the Factory Improvement Toolkit and soft skills for business.
Beneficiaries are  VCCI&apos;s member companies, particularly small and medium enterprises, in compliance with evolving national and international labour and sustainability standards. Other stakeholders include government institutions, especially those involved in labour and business legislation, and future generations of entrepreneurs inspired by Viet Nam&#x2019;s new national direction on enterprise development.</narrative>
  </description>
